# WPF Architecture Rules

## Layer dependencies (enforced by LayerDependencyTests)

| Layer | May use | Must not use |
|-------|---------|--------------|
| Models | System, Newtonsoft.Json | Services, Utilities, Views |
| Utilities | Models, Services (ILogger) | Views |
| Services | Models, Utilities | Views |
| Views | Models, WPF | Services, Utilities |
| MainWindow/App | All layers | — |

Violation remediation: move logic to Services/ or Models/; inject via constructor.

## Code conventions

- Parse `visual-config.json` via `VisualConfig.Load()` — not raw JSON in Views
- Content paths only through `ContentLoader`
- Coordinate math in `Utilities/CoordinateMapper` and `CoordinateValidator`
- Use `ILogger` in Services; avoid `Console.WriteLine` in Services/Views (except FileLogger)
- Keep `.cs` files under 800 lines

## WPF specifics

- Code-behind: event wiring and UI updates only
- No business logic in XAML code-behind beyond delegation to Services
- Config changes: edit `visual-config.json` and verify `Models/VisualConfig.cs` still deserializes

